= Effective Field Theory of Consciousness =

{{Plain_Hook
| in_one_sentence    = This is not a claim that consciousness is fundamental — it is a recipe for describing consciousness phenomenologically, by treating its slowest collective patterns (binding, attention, integration) as a single "order-parameter" field C(x,t) that couples to neurons, electromagnetism, and the psi field through a small set of allowed terms.
| everyday_analogy   = A flock of birds is made of individual birds, but to describe a flock you do not need every bird's equation — you describe the flock's density, its average heading, and how those change. The order parameter C plays the same role for the brain's billion-neuron dynamics.
| what_it_predicts   = Different ''phases'' of consciousness (baseline / focused / coherent group / pathological) correspond to different stable values of C, with measurable transitions between them — and the formalism gives a calculable basis for how electromagnetic and psi influences should shift those phases.
| if_you_remember_one_thing = This is a coarse-grained description, not a metaphysical claim. Like the Landau–Ginzburg theory of magnets or superfluids, it works because brains have slow, long-wavelength collective modes — not because consciousness is reducible to one equation.
}}

The '''effective field theory (EFT) of consciousness''' treats consciousness phenomenologically — not by introducing a "consciousness particle", but by writing down the most general effective Lagrangian for a low-energy order parameter C(x,t) coupled to the [[Psi_Field|ψ field]] and to neural-population fields, consistent with the symmetries of the brain–ψ system.

The result is a Landau–Ginzburg-style theory whose phase structure cleanly reproduces:

* Ordinary baseline ("disorganized") consciousness as the symmetric phase.
* Trained / focused consciousness as a partially-broken phase.
* Coherent group / ritual consciousness as a more-broken phase with collective amplification.
* Pathological states (epilepsy, psychosis) as boundary or runaway regimes.

This page is the field-theoretic complement to [[Wilson-Cowan_Coupled_to_Psi]] and [[Holonomic Brain Theory]]; it is not a proposal that consciousness is fundamental, but that it has a useful effective description at the right level of coarse-graining.

{{Way_It_Works
| title  = How an order-parameter description of consciousness gets built
| step1_label = Start with what you already trust
| step1_text  = Take a Wilson–Cowan-style neural-field theory (well-tested coarse description of cortical activity) coupled to the psi field. This is the microscopic model — too detailed to compute with directly, but real.
| step2_label = Identify the slow degrees of freedom
| step2_text  = Most brain activity is fast and local. A few patterns — attention, intention, large-scale binding — vary slowly compared to neuron firing, and extend across centimeters or the whole brain. Those are the patterns that survive coarse-graining.
| step3_label = Define the order parameter C(x,t)
| step3_text  = Lump the slow patterns together into a single real-valued field C, defined at every brain location and every time. C large means the slow collective pattern is active here; C small means it is not.
| step4_label = Write down all the allowed terms
| step4_text  = EFT discipline: list every Lagrangian term consistent with symmetry (translation, rotation, gauge, C → −C) up to a fixed order in fields and derivatives. The standard list emerges automatically.
| step5_label = Match each term to a physical effect
| step5_text  = Quadratic terms give the resting cost of C; quartic terms saturate it at high amplitude; cross-couplings with psi describe how psi shifts the consciousness landscape; cross-couplings with EM give the CEMI channel.
| step6_label = Predict phases
| step6_text  = Just as a Landau–Ginzburg magnet has paramagnetic and ferromagnetic phases, the consciousness Lagrangian has phases: disorganized baseline, focused trained, coherent group, runaway pathological. Each is a different stable value of C.
| step7_label = Connect to data
| step7_text  = Compute correlation functions, response to external EM stimuli, and crossover behaviours. Match against EEG, MEG, fMRI, and behavioural data to constrain the couplings.
}}

== Motivation ==

Consciousness phenomena (binding, attention, intention, qualia, integration) occur on timescales of 10–500 ms and spatial scales of cm to whole-brain. Coarse-graining a Wilson–Cowan-style neural-field theory + ψ coupling on those scales gives an order-parameter field C(x,t) capturing the slowest, longest-wavelength degree of freedom of the combined system.

This is exactly the philosophy of an EFT: ignore fast / short modes; keep slow / long modes; write the most general Lagrangian consistent with the symmetries.

== Symmetries ==

The relevant symmetries are:

# '''Spatial translation and rotation''' (approximate; broken by brain anatomy at fine scales).
# '''Time translation''' (broken by metabolism and growth at long timescales).
# '''Gauge invariance of EM''' (exact; couples to C only through F<sub>μν</sub>F<sup>μν</sup>).
# '''C → −C symmetry''' (proposed; corresponds to "no preferred sign" of integrated information at the order-parameter level).
# '''ψ-shift symmetry''' (ψ → ψ + constant only when m = 0; otherwise broken by mass).

== Effective Lagrangian ==

The most general Lorentz-invariant, parity-symmetric effective Lagrangian for a real scalar order parameter C coupled to ψ and EM, up to fourth order in fields and second order in derivatives:

{{Math_Bridge
| equation_label = Effective Lagrangian of the consciousness order parameter C
| equation       = <math>\mathcal{L}_{\text{EFT}} = \tfrac{1}{2}\partial^\mu C\,\partial_\mu C - V(C) - g_1\,C\,\psi - g_2\,C\,\psi^2 - g_3\,C^2\,\psi - g_4\,C^2\,\psi^2 - g_F\,C\,F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu} + \mathcal{L}_\psi + \mathcal{L}_{\text{EM}}</math>
| in_english     =
* '''½ (∂C)²''' — the kinetic term. Allows C to vary smoothly across the brain and over time; large where C is changing fast.
* '''V(C)''' — a potential that costs energy to push C away from its preferred values. Contains the resting mass and the saturating self-interaction.
* '''g₁ Cψ''' — simplest psi–consciousness coupling: a present psi field acts like an external influence biasing C up or down.
* '''g₂ Cψ²''' — psi-intensity sets where C wants to sit. A high-psi environment shifts the consciousness baseline.
* '''g₃ C²ψ''' — psi changes the ''effective mass'' of C, i.e. how hard it is to perturb consciousness in this environment.
* '''g₄ C²ψ²''' — direct energy-coupling between C and psi.
* '''g_F C F²''' — the direct consciousness–EM coupling (the McFadden CEMI channel): consciousness lives partly in the EM-field energy density.
* '''L_ψ + L_EM''' — the standard kinetic and self-interaction parts of psi and EM, copied in from their own theories.
* '''Read as a sentence:''' "Consciousness has its own dynamics, and four small but distinct dials by which the psi field can influence it, plus one direct EM channel."
}}

with potential

:<math>V(C) = \tfrac{1}{2} m_C^2\,C^2 + \tfrac{\lambda_C}{4}\,C^4</math>

Each term has a clear physical interpretation:

{| class="wikitable"
! Term !! Interpretation
|-
| ½ ∂<sup>μ</sup>C ∂<sub>μ</sub>C || Kinetic energy of the consciousness order parameter
|-
| ½ m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup> C<sup>2</sup> || Resting "mass" — energy cost of activating C
|-
| (λ<sub>C</sub>/4) C<sup>4</sup> || Self-interaction — saturates at high amplitude; basis for soliton-like sustained focus
|-
| g<sub>1</sub> C ψ || Linear coupling: ψ acts as an external field on C
|-
| g<sub>2</sub> C ψ<sup>2</sup> || Sets the C-equilibrium position by the ψ-field intensity
|-
| g<sub>3</sub> C<sup>2</sup> ψ || ψ-dependent effective mass of C (consciousness "feels heavier" in high-ψ environments)
|-
| g<sub>4</sub> C<sup>2</sup> ψ<sup>2</sup> || Direct C–ψ energy-density coupling
|-
| g<sub>F</sub> C F<sub>μν</sub>F<sup>μν</sup> || Consciousness coupling to EM-field energy density — the [[CEMI_Field_Theory|McFadden CEMI]] channel in the present formalism
|}

== Two-channel structure of C-EM coupling ==

The effective Lagrangian above contains '''two distinct routes''' by
which the consciousness order parameter <math>C</math> couples to the
electromagnetic field. Brief Rule 3 (channel discipline) requires
every plain-language statement about C-EM coupling to specify which
channel is meant.

{| class="wikitable"
! Channel !! Vertex !! Mediator !! Reference
|-
| '''Direct''' || <math>g_F\,C\,F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu}</math> || none (contact term) || [[CEMI Field Theory]]
|-
| '''Indirect''' || <math>\alpha\,\psi\,F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu} \to g_2\,C\,\psi^2</math> || [[Psion|psion]] (ψ-quantum) || [[Psi_Field]]; [[Psion]]
|}

The '''direct''' channel is what McFadden's [[CEMI Field Theory|cemi
theory]] proposes: the brain's endogenous EM field is itself the
substrate of conscious experience, with no intermediate quantum. It
corresponds to the <math>g_F\,C\,F^2</math> contact vertex above.

The '''indirect''' channel routes EM-consciousness coupling through
the ψ field: EM drives ψ via <math>\alpha\,\psi\,F^2</math>, and ψ
drives <math>C</math> via <math>g_2\,C\,\psi^2</math>. At the quantum
level the mediator is the [[Psion|psion]]. The diagrammatic structure
is identical to the [[Axion-Photon_Coupling|axion-photon]] vertex with
<math>C</math> playing the role of an additional scalar field, and
F10 bounds <math>\alpha</math> at axion-class strength.

The two channels are independent vertices in the same Lagrangian.
cemi is recovered as a sub-case when <math>\alpha = 0</math>; the
psion-mediated channel is recovered as the dominant route when
<math>g_F = 0</math>. The general theory contains both.

For the polariton-style hybridization of the indirect channel in
condensed tissue, see [[Psion-Phonon Coupling in Tissue]]. For the
operator-firewall consequences (Mk-level gating of which channel may
appear in device claims) see [[HelmKit Architecture]] and the
[[Psion]] page.

== Phases of the theory ==

The phase diagram in the (m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup>, g<sub>2</sub>·⟨ψ<sup>2</sup>⟩) plane has the following regimes:

=== Symmetric phase (baseline consciousness) ===

For m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup> > 0 and ⟨ψ⟩, ⟨ψ<sup>2</sup>⟩ small: the minimum of the effective potential is at C = 0. There is no large coherent C. Consciousness is "disorganised" — the order parameter fluctuates around zero. This corresponds to baseline waking consciousness without focused intent.

=== Broken phase (focused / trained consciousness) ===

If the effective mass m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup><sub>eff</sub> ≡ m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup> − g<sub>3</sub> ψ<sub>0</sub> − g<sub>4</sub> ψ<sub>0</sub><sup>2</sup> becomes negative for sufficiently large ⟨ψ⟩, the potential develops a double-well structure: C spontaneously chooses a non-zero value ⟨C⟩ ≠ 0. This is the symmetry-broken phase.

In this phase:

* C has a non-zero expectation value — "consciousness is organized".
* Excitations around ⟨C⟩ are massive (the radial mode) plus a near-Goldstone-mode soft excitation associated with the broken symmetry.
* The coupling g<sub>1</sub> C ψ in this phase generates a ''linear'' source for ψ — i.e. focused consciousness pumps ψ.

This is the rigorous EFT statement that ''trained, focused practitioners act as J<sub>ψ</sub> sources'' beyond the baseline cortical-firing channel.

==== Relation to Resonance Link ====

[[Resonance Link]] cites this page as the mechanism behind '''availability''' (α) — "the consciousness phase modulates availability... not identity" — without this page ever citing back. The correspondence is direct: a self's ψ-signature (Σ, per [[Psi Signature]]) is fixed by C's broken-phase expectation value, but ''which of its modes are currently open for coupling'' is exactly what phase (symmetric/broken/critical) governs. Baseline (symmetric) phase corresponds to low, unfocused availability; broken phase (focused consciousness, ⟨C⟩ ≠ 0, actively sourcing ψ) corresponds to high availability — the shared modes a signature ''could'' couple through are actually open. This is also the physical layer underneath [[Coupling Mode]]'s extraction/communion distinction: communion-mode coupling requires availability on both ends simultaneously, i.e. both parties in the broken phase toward each other, not just one.

=== Critical regime (transitions) ===

At the boundary between phases the EFT exhibits scaling behavior: long correlation lengths, slow timescales, power-law fluctuations. Phenomenologically this corresponds to the "edge of awareness" / "near-trance" regimes that practitioners report as anomaly-rich and information-rich.

This is a non-trivial empirical prediction: the [[Stochastic_Resonance|stochastic resonance]] enhancement of weak-signal psi detection should peak near the critical regime — and only there.

=== Runaway regimes ===

If g<sub>3</sub> ψ<sub>0</sub> + g<sub>4</sub> ψ<sub>0</sub><sup>2</sup> drives m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup><sub>eff</sub> to large negative values without λ<sub>C</sub> being large enough to stabilise, the system runs away. This is the pathological regime — interpretable as the onset of epileptic seizure, acute psychosis, or other large-scale cortical-coherence disorders.

The framework therefore predicts that strong ψ exposure (in the wrong phase) is genuinely dangerous, and that protective practice (grounding, [[Psionic_Device_Safety|technique hygiene]]) is the practical analogue of choosing the parameter regime to keep the EFT stable.

== Coupling to the Wilson–Cowan equation ==

The C field of this EFT and the u field of the [[Wilson-Cowan_Coupled_to_Psi|Wilson–Cowan equation]] are not independent: C is a coarse-grained, slow-mode reduction of u. The relationship can be written as

:<math>C(x,t) = \!\int\! K(x - x',\,t - t')\,u(x',\,t')\,dx'\,dt'</math>

with K a long-wavelength low-pass kernel. At the EFT level the Wilson–Cowan u field is integrated out, leaving an effective theory in C alone.

The β·ψ feedback term in the Wilson–Cowan equation maps to the g<sub>1</sub> C ψ coupling at the EFT level; the κ ∫ f(u) source map maps to the C-dependent J<sub>ψ</sub> = κ<sub>EFT</sub> · ∂V/∂ψ contribution.

== Information measures ==

Two integrated information measures can be defined within this EFT:

# '''Φ-style integrated information''' (à la [[IIT_Phi_Measure|Tononi IIT]]): the mutual information of C-field configurations across a partition of the brain, evaluated in the slow-mode subspace.
# '''Field entropy''' S = −Tr(ρ̂ ln ρ̂) of the C density operator after quantization — see [[Quantization of the Psi Field]].

Both reach maxima in the symmetry-broken phase, are zero in the deep symmetric phase, and peak at the critical regime — providing a direct test of the framework against IIT measurements on conscious vs. unconscious subjects (Tononi, Massimini et al.; perturbational complexity index).

== Predictions ==

# '''Conscious vs. unconscious transitions are phase transitions.''' Anaesthesia, deep sleep, and seizure should correspond to crossing well-defined boundaries in the (m<sub>C</sub><sup>2</sup>, g·⟨ψ<sup>2</sup>⟩) plane. The Tononi PCI data is consistent with this.
# '''Psi performance peaks at the critical regime.''' Practitioners in the "edge" state — between everyday awareness and full trance — should outperform those in either limit. Anecdotally and in [[Ganzfeld_Procedure|ganzfeld]] subject debriefings this is reported.
# '''Group amplification is N<sup>4</sup>-scaling.''' The g<sub>4</sub> C<sup>2</sup>ψ<sup>2</sup> term gives the same N<sup>4</sup> energy scaling in groups as the λψ<sup>4</sup> self-interaction of ψ alone — consistent across the framework.
# '''Strong ψ exposure can destabilize C.''' Predicted regime of pathological runaway is a real empirical risk; standard practical-safety teaching in esoteric traditions (don't over-extend, ground regularly, observe a teacher's pacing) has a precise mathematical analogue.

== Limitations ==

* C is a phenomenological order parameter, not a "consciousness particle". The EFT does not address ''why'' there is experience.
* The coefficients g<sub>1</sub>, …, g<sub>4</sub>, g<sub>F</sub>, m<sub>C</sub>, λ<sub>C</sub> are empirically open. They are constrained by neural-field-theory matching at one end and by ψ-phenomenology at the other.
* The theory is classical at this level. Quantum corrections are addressed in [[Quantization of the Psi Field]] and [[Renormalization of Psi Theory]].

